# Kame mascot rules

Assets: `ui/public/assets/mascot/` (93 transparent 448×468 PNG poses; `manifest.json`, `README.md`, `gallery.html`). Full spec: `docs/workflow/for-testing/mobile-native-app-redesign-design-system.md` §12.

**A mascot must have a job.** It never replaces a label, status icon, source, warning or review control.

## Roles

| Role                    | Size        | Poses                                                                                                                         | Where                                                                                                      |
| ----------------------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Welcome and orientation | 96 to 128px | `hello`, `happy-hop`, `install-app`, `sign-in`                                                                                | First-entry welcome (once per session), onboarding start, empty workspace, sign-in and install prompts     |
| Daily guidance          | 48 to 64px  | `dashboard-overview`, `explaining`, `arrival`, `parking-guide`                                                                | Today summary card only (property, parking, org); guest trip progress card                                 |
| AI identity             | 24 to 32px  | `ai-assistant`, `listening`, `thinking`, `explaining`                                                                         | Kame button, Ask Kame sheet, AI draft label, insight cards, conversation summary                           |
| Empty or recovery       | 72 to 96px  | `page-not-found`, `something-went-wrong`, `offline`, `coming-soon`, `rainy-day`, plus the domain pose matching the empty page | First-use empty states, 404, error boundary, offline screen, full-page plan gates                          |
| Milestone               | 96 to 128px | `booking-confirmed`, `action-success`, `delighted`, `room-key`, `guest-review`                                                | Guest booking submitted, review submitted, SD refund submitted, onboarding complete, verification approved |
| Setup incomplete        | 48 to 64px  | `workspace-settings`, `properties`, `parking-listings`                                                                        | Settings setup-health card, one listing needing setup                                                      |

Seasonal poses (`halloween`, `christmas-parol`, `valentine`, `new-year`, `easter`) only in the welcome role, behind a date-bounded flag.

## Budget

- At most **one** mascot per screen (an AI avatar in a thread counts as one).
- Dense operational screens (Bookings, Finance, Pricing, Inbox list, Activity, Team, Settings sections, all super-admin): **only** empty states and AI avatars.
- Filtered-empty results ("No bookings match") use text and "Clear filters", no mascot.

## Never

Tab bar · app bar · scope chip · metric tiles · list rows · calendar cells · charts · form fields or form screens · destructive confirms · payment, payout, refund amounts · legal, security, verification-rejected · critical announcements · whole-page loading · filler "tips" banners.

## Implementation

- Render through **`KameMascot`** only (`pose`, `role`, `decorative`). No raw `<img src="/assets/mascot/...">`, no CSS background.
- WebP variants at 96 / 160 / 320w with `srcset`, explicit `width` / `height`, `decoding="async"`, `loading="lazy"` (eager only on milestone screens). Never ship the 448px PNG in a list.
- `alt=""` when nearby text says the same thing (default); descriptive alt otherwise.
- Not in the shell precache; on-demand tier. Check the PWA budget after adding poses.
- One pose per role per screen; no perpetual animation. Milestone enter: scale 0.96 → 1 + fade, once, 240ms (fade only under reduced motion).
- The voice receptionist avatar (`ReceptionistAvatar`) is a separate feature and is not governed by this budget.
